[size=5][b]Accolade Workshop[/b][/size]

[size=5][b]At a glance[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]🟢 [b]Version 0.1.0[/b] · Targets CK3 [b]1.20.1.2[/b].
[*]🟢 [b]Standalone mod; requires Tours & Tournaments.[/b]
[*]🟢 [b]Create an accolade by choosing its attribute or its knight first.[/b]
[*]🟢 [b]Languages:[/b] English, French, German, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Russian, Simplified Chinese and Spanish.
[*]🔴 [b]Start a new campaign.[/b] Existing accolades have no migration for the rank-cap system.
[*]🔴 [b]Changes accolade ranks and two interface windows; overlapping mods need a compatibility patch.[/b]
[/list]

[size=5][b]Choose the honour, then the knight[/b][/size]

Looking for a particular accolade? Browse the attributes your court can provide, see how many candidates qualify, and choose the knight who will carry it. The familiar knight-first route remains available alongside it.

[size=5][b]Two ways to create an accolade[/b][/size]

The create button opens a choice of starting point:

[list]
[*][b]Attribute first:[/b] browse available initial attributes with candidate and guest counts. Select an attribute to see the eligible knights and guests.
[*][b]Knight first:[/b] use the familiar candidate list, then choose an eligible initial attribute.
[/list]

Both routes finish in the normal creation panel. The game's eligibility checks, recruitment costs, knight controls and accolade creation costs still apply. Guests must be recruited before creating their accolade.

[size=5][b]Set the highest rank[/b][/size]

The [b]Maximum accolade rank[/b] game rule offers [b]3, 6 (default), or 9[/b], for players and AI. Glory is capped at the chosen rank's threshold: 600, 2,100, or 4,500 respectively.

Ranks 7–9 provide further attribute upgrades. Accolades still have at most three attributes, each with three levels; the game's Men-at-Arms attribute restriction remains.

[size=5][b]Getting started[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Enable the mod and start a new campaign. Choose the maximum accolade rank in the game rules.
[*]Open the Military window, manage your knights and accolades, and click the accolade creation button.
[*]Choose your starting point, select a candidate and attribute, then confirm in the normal creation panel.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Compatibility and load order[/b][/size]

Requires [b]Tours & Tournaments[/b]; no other mod is required. Targets [b]CK3 1.20.1.2[/b].

Replaces [b]window_create_accolade.gui[/b] and [b]window_accolade.gui[/b], changes accolade rank definitions, and adjusts the accolade rank-change notification hook. Mods changing those same elements need a merged compatibility patch; load order alone does not merge them. Total conversions and multiplayer compatibility are not established.

[size=5][b]Saves and known limits[/b][/size]

[b]Use a new campaign.[/b] Existing accolades do not have the tracked Glory baseline required by the cap system. Migration and mid-campaign removal are not supported; keep a backup before changing a campaign's mod list.

Ranks 7–9 reuse the rank-6 badge ornament, with their own displayed rank names and numbers.

[size=5][b]Feedback and support[/b][/size]

Include your CK3 version, mod list, rank rule, chosen creation route and steps to reproduce the problem.

